messages:
pioneer_cto: Demo glitch — during today's POC the streaming chat stopped sending final tokens, client threw "Uncaught SyntaxError: Unexpected end of JSON input" and the browser never fired onmessage for the last SSE event. Happened twice (~20% of messages) during a 30m session. Need triage, customer on follow-up call tomorrow morning.

alana_sales: Ack — annoying. Can you paste the exact client console error and the request id from your logs? I’ll loop eng.

pioneer_cto: Console: "Uncaught SyntaxError: Unexpected end of JSON input at parse (<anonymous>):1:1" Also saw "EventSource failed" network error. Request-id in our app header: req_0ab1c2f3. HAR and small demo app uploaded to the drive link I DM'd.

keenan_support: Can you confirm which SDK version and browser? SSE SDK v0.9.1 had a known edge-case with partial chunk handling. Also, was there a proxy (nginx/ingress) in front?

pioneer_cto: Browser Chrome 118.0.5993, React wrapper around EventSource, SDK pinned at 0.9.1, running behind our nginx reverse-proxy.

jamal_eng: Quick look at the server logs for req_0ab1c2f3: I see the connection closed by upstream with "upstream prematurely closed connection" after ~15s. That smells like a proxy timeout or buffering issue causing mid-event truncation. Can you share nginx conf?

maria_devx: We’ve reproduced similar symptoms: if the server-stream sends an event that gets split across TCP packets and the client tries to parse each chunk as a full JSON message, you get "Unexpected end of JSON input". SDK v0.9.4 fixes the parser to accumulate data until the SSE event delimiter. Short-term workaround: upgrade SDK or adjust client to buffer until a blank line.

pioneer_cto: We can’t upgrade the SDK mid-demo easily. Can you share a minimal client-side change we can patch in our wrapper now?

jamal_eng: Minimal workaround (pseudo):

```js
// client-side buffering pseudo
let buf = ''
es.onmessage = (e) => {
  buf += e.data + '\n'
  // only try parse when we see event delimiter (blank line)
  if (e.data.endsWith('\n') || e.data === '') {
    try {
      const msg = JSON.parse(buf)
      handle(msg)
      buf = ''
    } catch (err) {
      // incomplete, wait for more chunks
    }
  }
}
```

Also enable retry/heartbeat on the SSE client so reconnects are smoother. We’ll ship an SDK hotfix but this buys time.

maria_devx: And check proxy settings — set `proxy_buffering off;` and increase `proxy_read_timeout` in nginx so upstream won’t close mid-stream. If you're using a cloud LB, ensure idle timeouts are > stream length.

pioneer_cto: Infra turned off buffering and increased timeouts, retested — partials dropped to ~2% but still seeing occasional truncated frames. Anything else we should check?

keenan_support: At 2% it's likely a client-side race on parse + intermittent TLS renegotiation or very short TCP resets. Add defensive retry for JSON parse errors: on parse failure, stash the raw chunk and wait up to N ms for more data before showing error. Also check for HTTP 429s from our side in your logs — a sudden backlog could lead to abrupt upstream closes.

alana_sales: Quick pricing question from the customer: if we temporarily switch to polling fallback during their POC, how will that affect billing? (short)
jamal_eng: Polling will increase token usage proportionally to the number of polls; engineering can estimate delta if you share expected poll frequency and session lengths. Finance/sales can provide pricing delta.

sre-bot: deploy job #4921 completed: sdks/v0.9.4 deployed to staging at 2026-03-20T22:13:00Z :white_check_mark:

jamal_eng: We'll prepare a hotfix for the React wrapper and cut a 0.9.4 patch containing the buffered parser tonight. Can you test tomorrow at 10:00 UTC?
pioneer_cto: Yes — we’ll run a 10:00 UTC session and send request-ids for any failures. Thanks all, appreciate the quick turnaround. :pray:
